  "body": "Keep adaptive expert caching and pipelined decode active while making cache updates follow accepted tokens. Rejected draft rows and discarded speculative windows no longer influence this opt-in policy. Windows stop at a token boundary; commits and drafts drain, then cache copies finish before the next block starts.\n\nDepends on #1656 (multi-stage pipeline, inspiration for this work) and #1674 (one-token commit fix). Their commits are included separately until merged. The new change is 148 insertions / 2 deletions in generate.cpp and MULTI_GPU.md. Related residency-publication work: #1517.\n\nEnable with `STRATA_ADAPT_BARRIER_TOKENS=64`, `STRATA_IQ_MT_MIN=1`, `--adapt-every 1 --adapt-swaps 80 --adapt-decay 0.97 --pipeline-windows 2 --pcie-frac 0`. The token interval replaces the window cadence; updates block even with adapt-async enabled. Unset/0 preserves existing behavior. CUDA/HIP serve mode only, distinct-GPU layer split; batch and helper/peer tiers are rejected. SYCL is unchanged. `STRATA_TRACE_ADAPT=1` records usage/residency hashes at each boundary.\n\n### 3x Tesla P4 results\n\nQwen3.8-Flash-Next IQ3_XXS, int8 KV, split 19/37, 27 CPU workers, greedy, spec 2, floor 0.5, identical starting expert IDs and request history, no prompt reuse. Prompts: Python merge, refrigerator prose, European capitals (34/27/22 input tokens). Each process warms all three at 128 output tokens; primary measured cap 256. Decode tok/s excludes startup/prefill.\n\n| 64-token / 80-swap policy | Code | Prose | Capitals | Median |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Serial |25.112|23.095|23.687|23.687|\n| Pipeline |40.054|26.479|28.300|28.300|\n| Pipeline repeat |40.173|26.445|28.253|28.253|\n| Forced rollback |23.355|21.737|22.116|22.116|\n\n18/18 token comparisons and all boundary hashes matched the same-policy serial reference, including warmups. Each arm performed 720 measured swaps; the forced arm exercised 428 rollbacks.\n\nOdd-boundary check (17 tokens / 160 swaps, output cap 128): another 12/12 exact comparisons, 2,381 measured swaps per arm and 203 forced rollbacks. Serial/pipeline/forced medians: 22.737/27.403/21.387 tok/s. Total: **30/30**. Default-off regression: **3/3** exact versus the prior build. CUDA and HIP builds passed; the separate unchanged SYCL engine also built.\n\nThese measurements used the integration build, which also contained public prefill-cache work. This branch excludes that unrelated work; the adaptive patch is unchanged (verified patch identity). Timing is a correctness screen: one serial pass and two normal pipeline passes, not a statistical benchmark. Sampled decoding, long contexts and multi-GPU HIP inference remain untested.\n\nThe original static serial/pipeline mismatch was reproduced on the old validated binary and disappeared with matched starting placement. This does not establish a remaining copy-corruption bug or promise equal outputs across different placement/adaptation policies.\n",
